        "why": "The parts sit in a fixed order from the tip backwards — apical cup, then the organelles, then the nucleus — so drawing them in that order fixes the internal plan in the memory.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Drawing the nucleus at the pointed anterior tip. The apical cup is at the tip; the nucleus lies behind the middle.",
          "Drawing a round cell. The sporozoite is long and sickle shaped.",
          "Leaving the pellicle unlabelled. It is the outer covering and carries a mark."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Draw one long curved body first, then fill it from the tip backwards: cup, organelles, Golgi, nucleus.",
        "margin_note": "Label the apical cup, secretory organelles, pellicle, Golgi complex, nucleus, mitochondrion and microtubules."
